   "html": "<p>To help promote The Weeknd’s first feature length film <em>Hurry Up Tomorrow</em>, we created a striking installation showcasing a towering 18’ bust with a mirrored face, designed to invite audiences into an unexpected and immersive encounter.</p>\n<p>During the day, viewers saw their own reflections within Abel’s shroud. At night, a concealed screen played a haunting series of shifting faces of the main cast, each seemingly battling for control. The visual narrative unfolded through with cinematic lighting, rolling fog and music, for an exciting installation that pulled fans into the film’s ominous atmosphere.</p>"
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "THE BUILD",
   "pieces": [
    {
     "type": "text2",
     "left": "<p>The installation was inspired by contemporary art practices that blur the lines between sculpture and digital illusion. Approaching the installation as both sculpture and stage, we built advanced projection and lighting technology within the carefully crafted structure.</p>",
     "right": "<p>Drawing from the film’s exploration of fractured identity and blurred realities, the build was conceived as a physical embodiment of Abel’s shifting persona. Surrounding the installation were bold visual elements, including signage, billboards, and interior fabric wraps.</p>"
    },
